 She said what needed to be said.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 6115}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVQozlHW", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 22, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8851842, "raw_content": "", "author": "ArthurJ", "created": 1790173197406, "profile_picture": "2n7j40CvvfEB", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Moebius", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.lifesitenews.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVQozlHW.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.lifesitenews.com/news/euthanasia-killing-of-christian-grandmother-now-under-criminal-investigation/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Euthanasia killing of Christian grandmother now under criminal investigation. A great-grandmother with cognitive decline was euthanized in Canada despite previously refusing due to her Christian beliefs, and the case is sparking global outrage. Law enforcement in Canada is now investigating.", "last_comment_created": 1790177163508, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 22, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A great-grandmother with cognitive decline was euthanized in Canada despite previously refusing due to her Christian beliefs, and the case is sparking global outrage.", "large_image": "3tZeXQ1kuNHLOUxZ.png", "title": "Euthanasia killing of Christian grandmother now under criminal investigation - LifeSite"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVQoyw4I", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 42, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8851532, "raw_content": "There are four close races in California. We need to devote time and money to winning them. I know there have been some disappointments, cough Iran, oil prices, but there have been big wins too. BORDER SECURITY. but the biggest red pill is, if we lose the Democrats get stronger.  We need to stand and fight.  I put links to their campaign sites. Pick one close to you and volunteer or contribute money. \n\n__22nd Congressional District (Central Valley):__ Held by Republican incumbent [David Valadao](https://valadaoforcongress.com/), facing a strong challenge from Democrat Randy Villegas in a majority-Latino district that remains a top toss-up/flip target.\n\n**48th Congressional District (San Diego and Riverside Counties):** An open toss-up seat after Republican Darrell Issa announced his retirement, triggering a competitive battle featuring local leaders Democrat Marni von Wilpert and Republican [Jim Desmond](https://www.desmondforcongress.com/)\n\n**27th Congressional District (Northern Los Angeles County):** A razor-thin Southern California swing district where Democratic incumbent George Whitesides faces Republican [Jason Gibbs](https://www.jasongibbsforcongress.com/) following a tight primary.\n\n**13th Congressional District (San Joaquin/Stanislaus Counties):** A high-stakes rematch where Democratic Rep. Adam Gray (who won by a microscopic margin in 2024) faces Republican former Stockton Mayor [Kevin Lincoln](https://www.kevinlincolnforcongress.com/)", "author": "SuperDuperBasedMD", "created": 1790160491446, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "DEUSVEULT232", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Cali pedes it's time to stand and fight.", "last_comment_created": 1790174642831, "content": "<p>There are four close races in California. We need to devote time and money to winning them. I know there have been some disappointments, cough Iran, oil prices, but there have been big wins too. BORDER SECURITY. but the biggest red pill is, if we lose the Democrats get stronger.  We need to stand and fight.  I put links to their campaign sites. Pick one close to you and volunteer or contribute money.</p>\n<p><strong>22nd Congressional District (Central Valley):</strong> Held by Republican incumbent <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://valadaoforcongress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">David Valadao</a>, facing a strong challenge from Democrat Randy Villegas in a majority-Latino district that remains a top toss-up/flip target.</p>\n<p><strong>48th Congressional District (San Diego and Riverside Counties):</strong> An open toss-up seat after Republican Darrell Issa announced his retirement, triggering a competitive battle featuring local leaders Democrat Marni von Wilpert and Republican <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.desmondforcongress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Jim Desmond</a></p>\n<p><strong>27th Congressional District (Northern Los Angeles County):</strong> A razor-thin Southern California swing district where Democratic incumbent George Whitesides faces Republican <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.jasongibbsforcongress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Jason Gibbs</a> following a tight primary.</p>\n<p><strong>13th Congressional District (San Joaquin/Stanislaus Counties):</strong> A high-stakes rematch where Democratic Rep. Adam Gray (who won by a microscopic margin in 2024) faces Republican former Stockton Mayor <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.kevinlincolnforcongress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Kevin Lincoln</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_